A||N||4||Seanh||Screwed up timing, how to reset?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||03-18-2001||07:21 PM||||Im intelegent. I started doing valve lash the other day and didnt put my distributor back in. How do I set it up first off, so the car will run somewhat? One other thing, where do I find the timeing mark on the vibration dampener? I cant see it anywhere. How do you see it with all that stuff in the way, I cant see a thing past the water pump. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||03-18-2001||07:57 PM||||Since you don't know where you are in the crank rotation you will need to establish top dead center(TDC). It helps to see the crank by removing the wheel but you don't have to. Looking from the bottom rear you can see and touch the crank. If you take the wheel off and the rubber fender well skirt, you can put a wrench on the end of the crank to turn it. With an assistant, put a screwdriver in the number one spark hole and feel the piston coming up to TDC as the crank is turned. Once TDC is found, you will see the correct timing mark on the crank. Mark it clearly. You will now be able to see it from above. Now you need to get the distributor in correct position so that the number one piston is firing. Locate the number one plug wire so you will know which way the distributor rotor should point. Since you won't see the rocker valves to know if this is the compression stroke or firing stroke it might be possible that the distribtor will be 180 out of position. If it doesn't try to fire either pull out and turn the distributor 180 degrees or rotate the plug wires 180 degrees. Once it is running you can put a timing light on it to set the timing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||03-18-2001||08:11 PM||||Go under car and you'll see a groove in the dampner. Mark it with white chalk. Romove #1 spark plug. Either block hole with finger or screw in a compression tester. When pressure increases you are on the compression stroke. Adjust timing mark to "0" (the deepest "V" on the timing mark plate) Then install distributor where the #1 terminal of the distributor is barely clockwise from where the rotor is pointing. This should be close enough to start the car.||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||03-18-2001||08:52 PM||||I like you method Orief. Seanh, just be careful marking the crank, I think there were four different grooves on my pulley.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wolfhound||03-18-2001||09:23 PM||||The correct groove is wide the others thinner.||||reg||1
